{"name":"Serrano Pepper","hex":"#556600","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"serrano pepper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A chili pepper of species Capsicum annuum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serrano_pepper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Serrano pepper","blocks":[{"text":"The serrano pepper is a type of chili pepper that originated in the mountainous regions of the Mexican states of Puebla and Hidalgo. The Scoville rating of the serrano pepper is 10,000 to 25,000. The name of the pepper is a reference to the mountains (sierras) of these regions. The pepper is commonly used to make hot sauces."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Serranochilis.jpg/330px-Serranochilis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serrano_pepper","wikidata":"Q617583"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Starr_070730-7846_Capsicum_annuum.jpg/500px-Starr_070730-7846_Capsicum_annuum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Starr_070730-7846_Capsicum_annuum.jpg/1280px-Starr_070730-7846_Capsicum_annuum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Starr_070730-7846_Capsicum_annuum.jpg/500px-Starr_070730-7846_Capsicum_annuum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Close-up of unripe serrano peppers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStarr_070730-7846_Capsicum_annuum.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}